# HexaTrack Cursor Rules

## Read First
- docs/READ_FIRST.md
- docs/CURRENT_TASK.md
- docs/MASTER_REQUIREMENTS.md

## Stack
- Frontend: Next.js 15, TypeScript, Tailwind, Zustand, Framer Motion, Lucide React, Zod
- Backend: ASP.NET Core, EF Core, Hangfire, Redis, JWT
- Database: PostgreSQL

## Design Tokens

| Token | Value | Use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `background` | `#0B1015` | App/page background |
| `surface` | `#121A22` | Cards, sheets, panels |
| `primary` | `#4F8CFF` | Primary CTA and selected state |
| `expense` | `#FF5C75` | Expense and destructive state |
| `success` | `#1FD18B` | Income and positive state |
| `border` | `rgba(255,255,255,0.06)` | Dividers and card borders |
| `textPrimary` | `#F5F7FA` | Primary text |
| `textMuted` | `#8B9BB4` | Secondary text |


## Rules

- Do not invent colors, gradients, shadows, spacing, icons, charts, copy tone, or navigation.
- Use approved tokens and reusable components first.
- No neon, heavy gradients, broad glassmorphism, decorative charts, horizontal scroll, nested tabs, emoji icons, or motivational finance copy.
- Max 1 primary CTA per section.
- Max 1 main graph per screen.
- Max 2 hierarchy levels.
- Dashboard max: 1 summary strip, 1 trend chart, 1 category visualization, 5 recent transactions, 1 AI insight.


## Finance Trust
- Store money as decimal(12,2), never float.
- Use idempotency keys on transaction creates.
- Wrap financial writes in DB transactions.
- Validate workspace, account, category, and permission before saving.
